{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/781611-writing-help-first-age-mortals-becoming-second-age-solars","id":781611,"title":"[Writing Help] First Age mortals becoming Second Age solars","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-07T02:01:46-08:00","id":781611,"title":"[Writing Help] First Age mortals becoming Second Age solars","content":"I'd like to tell a 3rd edition story for players entirely or mostly unfamiliar with Exalted, with the plot hook being that their characters lived in the First Age as normal mortals, but through some magical sci-fi plot twist they survive into the Age of Tumult and gain Solar exaltations there. I could use some help from setting veterans figuring out how to get my players from the First Age to the Second Age though.<br /> <br /> My current thought is that the characters all died in the First Age, but due to illegal soul modification experiments happening at that time their souls were harvested before passing into Lethe, stored, and eventually transmitted into willing mortal host bodies in the Second Age by cultists trying to resurrect the glories of the First Age. Would such souls still be valid targets for Exaltation in 3e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T02:13:51-08:00","id":781617,"title":"","content":"What's the goal behind first age mortals? Could it not be done through another channel such as a assist carrying memories of its first age incarnation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8659-cyron","name":"Cyron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8659_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T02:25:08-08:00","id":781618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cyron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/781611-writing-help-first-age-mortals-becoming-second-age-solars?p=781617#post781617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the goal behind first age mortals? Could it not be done through another channel such as a assist carrying memories of its first age incarnation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Good question. I want to tell a &quot;fish out of water&quot; story for players that don't know a lot about the setting while also exploring the reasons the Solars were sealed. With this I can explain the core settings elements (magitech, gods, the celestial hierarchy, etc) while leaving the details unknown before dropping my players into a world that is both unknown and very very hostile since they are &quot;First Age Solars&quot; and therefore first priority targets for a lot of interesting antagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","user":"kindledRadial","date":". 12-07-2015, 05:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T02:51:27-08:00","id":781620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/781611-writing-help-first-age-mortals-becoming-second-age-solars?p=781618#post781618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With this I can explain the core settings elements (magitech...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Your Creation sounds pretty different from mine. Not sure how I can help.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T03:09:33-08:00","id":781626,"title":"","content":"3rd Edition is getting rid of a lot of the magitech as being a given. Granted, you can certainly have it in your game, and I'm pretty sure that it has been explicitly stated that no one would of been able to experience all of the First Age personally due to sheer vastness of Creation at the time so there is very much room for them to have been in an area of the First Age that had that in a high amount. As for how... something that could of happened is that they were about to Exalt when the Jade Prison happened and it took their mortal souls with the Exaltations as the still trying to join them. As nothing can separate you from your Exaltation other then death, the Exaltation getting trapped in the Jade Prison right as it attaches to you would, in a way, make a strange sort of sense. The harder part would be why they were all Exalting at the same time in the First Age and right around each other. As for your idea for soul modification experiments... it would depend on if the souls still counted a 'human' I think, as that is the only requirement I can think of for Solar Exaltation with regards to the soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9034-bulshock","name":"Bulshock","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T11:42:47-08:00","id":781768,"title":"","content":"I wrote magitech as an example, mostly because I had assumed it a given based on my 2E understanding of the First Age, but it's actually not that important that it be included to me. The important part is that they were raised in a utopia designed by the Solar exalted but now find themselves in a much harsher world with all the power they need to rebuild those days if they wish, albeit against considerable opposition.<br /> <br /> Bulshock: a fine suggestion, though if possible I'd like to run a first session in which they are briefly mortal tier in the Second Age so they will be exposed to all the horror that normal people endure in the Age of Sorrow before being imbued with god-tier powers. As for the simultaneous exaltation, my thought is that in 3E Sol seems to be a much more active component for who gets a Solar exaltation, and he chooses the party en mass to form a circle because he wants to see if the morals and convictions of the Age of Wonders will be a balm or an affliction for Creation.<br /> <br /> All: the question of how to get normal mortal souls from the end of the First Age into the end of the Second is the big narrative device I need help with. I'm pretty sure that most &quot;immortal&quot; humans no longer qualify for exaltation, and I'm concerned that with what I have now the souls wouldn't qualify normally. I could just have the player character's frozen in Elsewhere, maybe as a result of a Dragonblooded terrorist attack, but I'd rather do something that will highlight something cool about Creation's lore and setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T11:55:44-08:00","id":781772,"title":"","content":"They were important people (at least to some random exalt who happened to like their face, voice, whatever) who were frozen in preparation for a transplant or similar procedure.<br /> Then, of course, the Usurpation happened and they've only recently been awoken, be it by chance, archeologists or fate. They'd still be needing their individual procedures to have any chance to live for a long time. Of course, the procedure is rendered unneeded by the exaltation, but they don't know that while they strive to learn the savages' language and try to figure out what to do now.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, they might have been convicts who were being transported in stasis, or been part of an experiment involving stasis etc. .<br /> Maybe they were part of the crew of a first age wyld exploration vessel, which has just now returned from it's (to them) five year journey to realize their vessel wasn't quite what was promised, since thousands of years have passed in Creation. Not only must they now face a fallen age, their careers are done for, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2UIUH9oaJnHMWIxcVdGMjNUYlE\" target=\"_blank\">3EX Martial Arts basic overview (Weapons, Armor, Attributes &amp; Abilities)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/366-edward-eldritch","name":"Edward Eldritch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T11:56:24-08:00","id":781774,"title":"","content":"A Vision of Gold Supporter survives the Night of Fallen Stars (or whatever the kill all the gold faction supporters event was called). She realizes she can not stop the Usurpation, so she takes your PCs (who are newly Exalted Solars and thus not known to the other Sidereals yet) and locks them in stasis outside of Fate. The idea is that after a hundred years or so, the Sidereal will break them out and the Solars will pick up the pieces of Creation after the Usurpation. Unfortunately, the Sidereal does not make it back to the Fate Stasis Chambers, so the PCs are stuck in stasis until *insert plot element here* occurs.<br /> <br /> Now you got a bunch of First Age Solars with little or no training wandering around the Second Age. Due to the effects of Arcane Fate, they probably have no clue who put them in the Stasis Chambers or why.<br /> <br /> A bit of a Magitechy solution with some weird plot holes, but I think Newly Exalted Solars would be more likely to survive than Mortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T12:13:35-08:00","id":781785,"title":"","content":"This is originally for 2e game... One PC is Abyssal Half-Caste, made in First Age via some fetal manipulation using Black Mirror. The mirror was borrowed by her Solar maker for the occasion and he could not replicate her without it. Her children and clones all ended up mortal or half-solars. When she fell out of favor*, she was put in &quot;crio-chamber&quot; for preservation. She was found by Lookshy Sorcerer-Engineers ten years before &quot;year one&quot;.<br /> <br /> *There was little more to it, but that's the short version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1673-runelord","name":"Runelord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1673_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T12:18:00-08:00","id":781786,"title":"","content":"Good ideas all around, thanks for everything so far! Offline I also heard &quot;placed in emergency elsewhere stasis as part of a Solar defense system against terrorist attack&quot; and &quot;being placed in stasis at the time of exaltation might just be what the Jade Prison IS&quot; which I'm also considering. Further ideas encouraged!<br /> <br /> I have a couple story hooks already but I'd love more if people can think of fun stories to tell using culture shocked First Age Solars as a plot device. First session will involve them being woken up by Solar doomsday cultists who are led by a Dark Path Dragon King who is hoping to revive Solars, not mortals, and feeds the &quot;failures&quot; to unenlightened Raptok, prompting the party's mass exaltation. They will only know of enlightened Dragon Kings being from the First Age, so I'll be able to play up their confusion with these antagonists. Plus, if they keep him alive, the cult's ringleader might actually be able to fill them in on what they've missed over the last age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T12:29:01-08:00","id":781790,"title":"","content":"A base located in elsewhere, whose &quot;time generating device&quot; got destroyed in Usurpation. Thousands of years later, someone finds a way to access it and recover the survivors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1673-runelord","name":"Runelord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1673_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T12:32:18-08:00","id":781791,"title":"","content":"I'd have the PCs emerge from stasis at the beginning of the game.<br /> <br /> Either magitech cryogenic sleep or some kind of magical faerieland where time passes veeeery slooowly. Either works.<br /> <br /> They were placed there for science or by accident or to keep them alive longer or to keep them safe from some kind of threat or because someone thought they might be useful later. The Usurpation prevented their planned release, or maybe they were always meant to be in there for thousands of years. Regardless, they're out now.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Massively scooped. That's what I get for leaving a post window open for an hour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T17:11:18-08:00","id":781950,"title":"","content":"In the First Age, one of the Sun's Chosen was an investigator of unparalleled skill. He sought ever to hone this skill, perfecting it so that no clue could escape him. But he found that, while he could detect and interpret nearly any sign, one thing still stood against him.<br /> <br /> Change.<br /> <br /> The world is ever in motion. A breeze wipes away the last faint trace of the courtesan's perfume. A note, scrawled on a wall in charcoal, dissolves in the rain. A flustered official gets a few moments to calm down and rehearse a subtle lie.<br /> <br /> To one who stood astride the world, whose will could be gainsaid only by his glorious peers, this was an unbearable affront. He poured himself into the work of seizing that which a changing world would deny him. Though he never fully succeeded, over the course of a thousand years his efforts yielded many wonders, some discovered, some created. Of the latter, the greatest is probably a artifact called Truth's Arrestor. With it, an Exalt may cast an effect over an area which puts it in stasis. It does not freeze time itself, for what is time except a reference by which all things exist? Instead, it robs everything everything under its effects of the ability to change. This effect can be dismissed all at once, or piecemeal as the artifact's bearer experiences and considers every square inch with utmost care. It also protects from change imposed by the outside world. Only magic of equal potency can break the effect.<br /> <br /> Though it was indeed a powerful tool for investigating, it in practice proved most useful as a trap. What better way to catch a thief than to lock them into stasis right as their hands touch your most prized possession?<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> This gives a number of openings for your PCs to be trapped. Were they caught up in an investigation, which never completed, of a crime which the may or may not have been participating in? Did Truth's Arrestor activate to catch them looting in the chaos just after the Usurpation? Did a Sidereal realize that it could, in fact, just be used as a stasis machine and use it to put the PCs on ice for their own purposes?<br /> <br /> As for waking up, someone else could have deactivated the artifact (perhaps that same Sidereal?). Or perhaps at long last it has failed, as many artifacts have done since the Solars were overthrown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Angel Toaster from Keychain of Creation.","edited":{"userid":7935,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7935-cartographer7","user":"Cartographer7","date":".  Minor grammar edit. 12-07-2015, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7935-cartographer7","name":"Cartographer7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7935_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T23:21:55-08:00","id":782103,"title":"","content":"What about post-first-session stuff? Culture shock with the Second Age would be a recurring joke, I think. Learning that the Haltans and Linowans have been warring for centuries over tree planting rights (something First Age diplomacy would never allow) could spawn a whole game by itself. Any other big culture shocks they might be in for?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-07T23:35:40-08:00","id":782108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/781611-writing-help-first-age-mortals-becoming-second-age-solars?p=782103#post782103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any other big culture shocks they might be in for?</div> </div> </div> </div>The gods extorting worship out of mortals should be more than a bit unsettling. Heaven and the spirit courts were drastically less corrupt.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T03:14:34-08:00","id":782184,"title":"","content":"Another way to bring First Age people into the Second age: Gens Isa's expedition. Havng traveled out jnto the Wyld (where time doesnt behave the same), it's possible they could just be returning now. This would be great on several levels, for example needing to send out scouts in order to find a place to set down (the original ports and cities these peole lanned to return to are long gone, and they need some place to go), and other ways of finding how the world has changed. And gives some drama of the crew ofmthe expedition trying to settlemin and figure out how to fit into ann unfamiliar world.<br /> <br /> This is one I wanted to use for a character I had in mind. He would need to be First Age born, since his father was an NPC from the First Age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T04:50:23-08:00","id":782226,"title":"","content":"Consider having them encounter the grand-grand-grand........-grandchildren of their younger brother, friendly uncle, town carpenter whatever, with him being a perfect look-alike and carrying a name that's at least close to the person they lost the chance to see grow up. This could easily be either used to underline how much time has gone by, with things still basically the same.<br /> <br /> While a bit heavy-handed you might also consider them tripping over another stasis-person, be it an exalt or not, who's basically bureaucracy's first casualty, having been forgotten in stasis long before their time. He could handily contrast their view of the world by being in optimistic awe at the simplest huts or slightly elaborate tools and probably finds a world without murderous breezes rather pleasant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2UIUH9oaJnHMWIxcVdGMjNUYlE\" target=\"_blank\">3EX Martial Arts basic overview (Weapons, Armor, Attributes &amp; Abilities)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/366-edward-eldritch","name":"Edward Eldritch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T06:59:46-08:00","id":782271,"title":"","content":"I'd say either some sort of weird first age tomb thing - perhaps a powerful sorcerous working put a Sorceror's favorite servants in stasis pending the return of their exaltation.<br /> <br /> Or they were from a town swallowed by the Wyld but protected somehow, only for it to re-emerge so much later in time, but for them only a terrifying night has passed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/448-dulahan","name":"Dulahan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T07:21:32-08:00","id":782291,"title":"","content":"Fish out of water effect may be achived by other <br /> means:<br /> - give PC amnesia <br /> - make their motral bodies cloned / produced in <br /> some facility (from first age) .. they get exalted just <br /> after training and entering service<br /> - make them peasants gnorant in world futher than day or two from their hamlet(espetially if was rather safe society and in remote / inacessible location)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4588,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4588-ludek","user":"Ludek","date":". 12-08-2015, 10:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4588-ludek","name":"Ludek","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T15:31:31-08:00","id":782532,"title":"","content":"Here's a story hook I could use suggestions for: a major city or town ruled by largely benign, helpful Creatures of Darkness. The mortals there were completely abandoned by all the &quot;good guys&quot; and had no one else to turn to; now the party has to come to terms both with the desperation the Usurpation caused and with the fact that traditional bad-guy good-guy roles have been jumbled together over the last few millennium. Any suggestion for a local?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-08T17:36:03-08:00","id":782565,"title":"","content":"They were test subjects for Dragon-King stasis cylinders, wit